  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $A\\subset\\mathbb{N}$ be an additive basis of order $k$ which is minimal, in the sense that if $B\\subset A$ is any infinite set then $A\\backslash B$ is not a basis of order $k$.\nMust there exist an infinite $B\\subset A$ such that $A\\backslash B$ is a basis of order $k+1$?\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"L1\"\n},{",
